  "_commit": {
    "id": "a1eb918d74f70a8767c5e69f8e026af1172e0b33",
    "author": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "committer": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "message": "fix: preserve factor columns in splitParquetPart() (0.99.22)\n\nDuckDB has no categorical/dictionary SQL type, so the temp-table round\ntrip flattened an Arrow dictionary-encoded column (how arrow::write_parquet()\nstores an R factor) to plain VARCHAR -- silently turning factors into\ncharacter, and discarding any level unused in the data outright (not\nrecoverable from the written values once that happens).\n\nFactor columns (including ordered ones and unused levels) are now\ndetected from the source file's schema before the DuckDB-based row split\nand restored on each output part afterward via a small, per-part\narrow-only read/rewrite. DuckDB still does the actual row splitting;\narrow only touches columns that need it, and only when factor columns\nare present.\n",
    "time": 1787116774
  },
